## 1. What Is RAG (Simplest Explanation)

**Core idea:** an LLM alone can't answer questions about your private data (e.g. "what's the home office reimbursement policy?") because it was never trained on it — it will hallucinate a generic answer. RAG fixes this by **retrieving** the relevant document, **augmenting** the prompt with it, then letting the LLM **generate** the answer.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Q[User Question] --> R[Retrieve relevant docs]
    R --> A[Augment prompt with context]
    A --> G[LLM Generates answer]
    G --> U[Response to user]

    style Q fill:#1e3a5f,stroke:#4a90d9,color:#fff
    style R fill:#2d4a2d,stroke:#5cb85c,color:#fff
    style A fill:#4a2d4a,stroke:#c95cc9,color:#fff
    style G fill:#5f3a1e,stroke:#d9a04a,color:#fff
    style U fill:#1e3a5f,stroke:#4a90d9,color:#fff
```

**Key insight:** RAG = automating something you already do manually (copy-pasting a policy doc into ChatGPT). The whole system exists to remove the human from that retrieval step.

