## 5. Vector Similarity (Dot Product)

Since 384-dimension vectors can't be visualized, similarity is computed mathematically:

1. Multiply corresponding vector components.
2. Sum the products.
3. Normalize to a 0–1 score.
4. Closer to 1 = more similar.

**Course example result:** "dogs" vs "pets" → 73.3% similar. "dogs" vs "remote" → 36.2%. This demonstrates the model understands **category**, not just spelling.

