## 9. Production Concerns: Caching, Monitoring, Error Handling

### 9.1 Caching
RAG is slow — embeddings + vector search + LLM calls can add up to ~1 second per query. Since many queries repeat, caching turns that into milliseconds.

| Cache type | Stores | Use case |
|---|---|---|
| Query cache | Full Q&A pairs | Exact repeated questions |
| Embedding cache | Computed vectors | Same chunk embedded multiple times |
| Vector search cache | DB query results | Similar queries → same chunks |
| LLM response cache | Generated answers | Most expensive to compute, most valuable to cache |

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Q[Query] --> Key[Hash query+context → cache key]
    Key --> Check{In Redis?}
    Check -->|Yes| Fast[Return cached response]
    Check -->|No| Pipeline[Run full RAG pipeline]
    Pipeline --> Store2[Store in Redis with TTL]
    Store2 --> Fast
```

**Insight:** TTL choice matters more than the course lets on. For policy documents that change quarterly, a long TTL is fine — but if your underlying source doc updates and you don't invalidate the cache key, users get **confidently wrong, stale answers**, which is arguably worse than no cache at all. Cache invalidation (not just expiration) should be tied to your document update pipeline, not just time.

### 9.2 Monitoring
Standard metrics: response time, throughput, error rate. RAG-specific metrics: retrieval quality (are the right chunks coming back?), embedding latency, chunking efficiency.

Tools mentioned: **Prometheus** (metrics), **Grafana** (dashboards), **Jaeger** (tracing), **ELK stack** (logging).

### 9.3 Error Handling — Graceful Degradation
This maps directly to the fallback pattern in your code snippet:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start[Query] --> Full[Try full RAG pipeline]
    Full -->|VectorDBError| KW[Fallback: keyword search]
    Full -->|LLMError| Chunks[Fallback: return raw retrieved chunks]
    Full -->|EmbeddingError| Text[Fallback: simple text matching]
    Full -->|Success| Answer[Return generated answer]
    KW --> Answer2[Formatted result]
    Chunks --> Answer2
    Text --> Answer2
    KW -->|also fails| Err[Generic error message]

    style Full fill:#2d4a2d,stroke:#5cb85c,color:#fff
    style Err fill:#5f1e1e,stroke:#d94a4a,color:#fff
```

**Important design idea highlighted in the transcript:** a **half-open circuit breaker** pattern — periodically retry the failed component in the background, and only resume normal operation once it succeeds again, instead of just retrying every single request against a known-broken service.

